# https://w3id.org/vcf-rdfizer/
#
# RETIRED namespace of the VCF-RDFizer Vocabulary, versions 1.0.x and 1.1.0.
# The vocabulary continues as the VCF Core Vocabulary at
# https://w3id.org/vcf-core/ so that the model is identified independently of
# any one converter.
#
# Maintainer: Elias Crum <elias.crum@ugent.be>
#             IDLab, Ghent University - imec, Belgium
# Source:     https://github.com/ecrum19/VCF-RDFizer-vocabulary
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT A REDIRECT TO THE NEW NAMESPACE. Every IRI under this
# namespace resolves to a legacy document in which that IRI is still defined,
# deprecated, and linked to its successor with owl:equivalentClass,
# owl:equivalentProperty or owl:sameAs. Redirecting to the new vocabulary would
# resolve a legacy IRI to a document that does not define it, which is less
# useful than a 404.
#
# The legacy document is generated once by scripts/migrate-namespace.mjs and is
# not extended with new terms.
#
# BEFORE OPENING THE PULL REQUEST: replace every REPLACE-ME below with the real
# publishing host, with no trailing slash, and confirm that host actually serves
# legacy-vcf-rdfizer.ttl. Test the rules against a local checkout first.

Options +FollowSymLinks
RewriteEngine on

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retired vocabulary. Fragment IRIs such as .../vocab#VCFFile dereference here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RewriteRule ^vocab/?$ REPLACE-ME/assets/legacy-vcf-rdfizer.ttl [R=302,L]
RewriteRule ^vocab\.ttl$ REPLACE-ME/assets/legacy-vcf-rdfizer.ttl [R=302,L]
RewriteRule ^vocab/[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+/?$ REPLACE-ME/assets/legacy-vcf-rdfizer.ttl [R=302,L]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retired instance IRI space. Never published; nothing to serve.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RewriteRule ^vcf/ - [R=410,L]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything else under the retired namespace: the deprecation record.
# A human visiting the bare namespace is sent to the successor's documentation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RewriteRule ^$ https://w3id.org/vcf-core/ [R=302,L]
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ REPLACE-ME/assets/legacy-vcf-rdfizer.ttl [R=302,L]
